# Shell scripts must always have LF line endings (CRLF breaks bash on Windows-mounted WSL paths,
# and this repo's .sh files are checked out CRLF without this rule).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Container rootfs overlays: scripts COPY'd straight into a Linux image, deliberately with no
# extension because that is the name they are exec'd by. `* text=auto` plus core.autocrlf=true
# (the Git-for-Windows default, and what this box has) rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and a
# `#!/bin/sh\r` shebang fails inside the container with "no such file or directory" naming an
# interpreter that plainly exists. They are LF in the working tree today, so this rule is what
# stops the next clone from being the one that breaks.
rails/*/deploy/rootfs/**/bin/* text eol=lf

# Everything else: let git use the platform default
* text=auto
